    [Performance] Enable fused MiniMax sparse prepare through 256K tokens (#18666)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it
    
    Forward-port of #18660 to `main`.
    
    MiniMax-M3's fused sparse-prepare path currently falls back to the
    separate Q/K normalization, RoPE, and cache-insertion chain whenever a
    batch contains more than 512 tokens. Raise the validated routing limit
    to 262144 tokens so prefill can use `minimax_qknorm_rope_cache`.
    Requests beyond the validated range retain the existing fallback.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce any user-facing change?
    
    No configuration change is required. Supported MiniMax-M3 BF16 NPU
    prefill batches up to 256K tokens now use the existing fused
    QK-norm/RoPE/cache-insert kernel.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - Patch is identical to #18660 (`git patch-id --stable`)
    - Release branch validation: `pytest -q
    tests/ut/models/minimax_m3/test_fused_sparse_prepare.py` (`23 passed`)
    - A3 large-prefill correctness and latency validation at 32K, 64K, 128K,
    and 256K tokens
    - Runtime validation with MiniMax-M3 prefill chunk size 2048
    - The `main` forward-port was not separately rerun, per request
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/c4df37dfcc7f72ca41cd43801a468526ecf99a2b
    
    Signed-off-by: qq_40172610 <chenchaofeng5@huawei.com>
    Co-authored-by: qq_40172610 <chenchaofeng5@huawei.com>

